1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,941
Every app starts with one
database.

2
00:00:03,091 --> 00:00:05,058
Then people actually show up.

3
00:00:05,757 --> 00:00:08,361
Traffic doubles. Then it doubles
again.

4
00:00:08,501 --> 00:00:10,543
And that's the part your users
feel.

5
00:00:10,683 --> 00:00:13,863
It works — until there's no
bigger machine to buy.

6
00:00:14,564 --> 00:00:16,064
So you split the data.

7
00:00:16,214 --> 00:00:21,272
Sharding cuts one huge table
into smaller pieces, each on its
own server.

8
00:00:21,412 --> 00:00:24,701
Now every server carries only a
slice of the load.

9
00:00:24,851 --> 00:00:27,287
Need more room? Add another
shard.

10
00:00:27,427 --> 00:00:29,725
So one database becomes many.

11
00:00:29,875 --> 00:00:31,697
Your app never notices.
